{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"civillaw-ecological-puffin","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered while diagnosing the 2026-07-31 `rebar-autodeploy-errors` alarm. This is the ORIGINATING\nevent for that incident; the reason it became unrecoverable is filed separately as\n304e-9c0f-2068-4d0e (the orphaned lock cannot be reclaimed inside a container).\n\nAt 18:30:48 UTC the review-bot container `1e0fab75d5bd` logged a completed store write\n(`code_review artifact 98a6-8110-6e39-48ce: linked 2/2 trailer refs`) and `Shutting down` in the SAME\nsecond, because an autodeploy cycle recreated it. It created the write-lock dir at 18:30:49 — AFTER\n`Finished server process` — and was SIGKILLed at ~18:30:55 still holding it.\n\n`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` declares no `stop_grace_period` for the review-bot service, so it\ngets docker's default 10s before SIGKILL. That is not reliably enough for an in-flight store write to\nfinish and release its lock, and the store is append-only with a mkdir lock whose release is the\nprocess's responsibility.\n\nThis is a latent hazard independent of how often deploys run — it simply became likely on a day with\nnine merges driving ~six container recreates in 90 minutes.\n\n## Approach\n\nGive the review-bot a `stop_grace_period` long enough for an in-flight store write to complete and\nrelease its lock, and confirm the service actually handles SIGTERM by finishing that write rather than\nexiting immediately. A grace period only helps if the shutdown path drains the write.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` — review-bot service `stop_grace_period`.\n- The review-bot's SIGTERM/shutdown handling, if it does not currently drain an in-flight store write.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The review-bot service declares a `stop_grace_period` exceeding the worst-case in-flight store\n      write, with the value justified rather than arbitrary.\n- [ ] A SIGTERM during an in-flight store write releases the write-lock before exit; verified by a\n      test or a documented reproduction that stops the container mid-write and shows no lock dir left\n      behind.\n- [ ] The deploy's blast-radius guarantee is unchanged (review-bot only; the gerrit container is not\n      restarted).","id":"1a47-61a4-a981-4398","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"review-bot has no stop_grace_period, so a deploy recreate can SIGKILL it mid-store-write and orphan the lock"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785527296356626001,"uuid":"84c5c9ca-fee6-48b1-887c-7b42cde06ae9"}